{"review":{"at":"2026-10-08T15:59:22-05:00","size":"light","verdict":"fix","findings":[{"n":1,"kind":"fix","text":"public/framework/ai/system-classes.js:240 — requirements.md says to find and reuse the existing class-doc mechanism (`ext/Doc`, which has Doc.js, decisions.js, page.js), and not to build a second. The diff adds a hand-written `CLASSES` list and `class_card()` instead, and findings.md never says why `ext/Doc` was not used. Either reuse or extend `ext/Doc`, or state the reason in findings.md."},{"n":2,"kind":"fix","text":"public/framework/ai/system-classes.js:303 — `live_agents()` fetches the hard-coded `http://localhost/api/agents` from a page served at `monorepo.localhost`. That is cross-origin, and it will fail unless Servex sends CORS headers on that route. I only saw `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` in 5 Servex files, and did not check `/api/agents`. In the static production site it always shows the \"not answering\" line. Confirm the route sends CORS headers, or resolve the Servex origin from config."},{"n":3,"kind":"fix","text":"requirements.md addendum item 1 — `systems-map.md` (a short table linked from `ai/readme.md`) is not in the diff, and neither is any skill or system-prompt study. If those are separate tasks, say so in findings.md. If not, the work is missing."},{"n":4,"kind":"fix","text":"public/framework/ai/readme.md:+2 and public/framework/ai/doc/architecture.md:+4 — the link text promises `Servex/doc/sdk.md` and `Servex/doc/architecture.md`, but the hrefs go to `/framework/servex/`. Link to the real pages, for example with `file_link`, as overview.js does for sdk.md."},{"n":5,"kind":"note","text":"public/framework/ai/overview.js:+195 — the Dashboard card links to `/framework/ai2/`, while findings.md says the root readme calls AI 2 retired. Check where this should point."},{"n":6,"kind":"note","text":"public/framework/ai/system-classes.js:240 — the API member lists were written by hand and I did not check them against the source. findings.md already suggests a script to check them (law 7). That script would be cheap and worth running before merge."},{"n":7,"kind":"note","text":"The diff shows no evidence of the four-width screenshots, the smoke test, or the diff review that requirements.md asks for. `Servex/doc/sdk.md` is honest about what it did not verify, which is good."},{"n":8,"kind":"note","text":"public/framework/ai/overview.js:+199 — wrapping the concept cards in `<details>` is a simple way to cut the page down. The old \"Who starts the agents\" block was dropped, but the SDK card and sdk.md cover it."}],"branch":"worktree/aisysdocs","head":"d8063d6950eb32a861b303870a82f117897f0700","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","cost":0.4370684000000001,"file":"review.md","report":null,"shots":null}}
